     "title": null,
     "text": "Whenever any non-linear function $f(\\cdot)$ (such as $\\sin(\\cdot)$, $\\cos(\\cdot)$, $\\exp(\\cdot)$, $(\\cdot)^2$, $\\ln(\\cdot)$, $\\operatorname{sgn}(\\cdot)$, $|\\cdot|$) encapsulates the input signal $x(t)$, both additivity and homogeneity are violated. The only function $f(u)$ that satisfies $f(u_1+u_2) = f(u_1)+f(u_2)$ and $f(\\alpha u) = \\alpha f(u)$ is the linear proportional relationship $f(u) = k \\cdot u$."
