     "type": "NOTE",
     "title": null,
     "text": "Attempting to define an inverse system as $x(t) = \\sqrt{y(t)}$ fails because the square root operator always yields the principal positive root, permanently losing negative input signals ($x(t) = -3 \\implies y(t) = 9 \\implies \\sqrt{9} = +3 \\neq -3$)."
