     "text": "**GATE Exam Insight: Finite Energy Does NOT Imply Absolute Integrability!**\nThis problem provides the reverse counterexample:\n- The energy converges because squaring accelerates the rate of asymptotic decay ($1/t^2$ decays fast enough for the area to equal $1$).\n- But the absolute signal $1/t$ decays too slowly as $t \\to \\infty$, causing the harmonic integral to diverge logarithmically ($\\ln \\infty = \\infty$).\n- Therefore: **Energy Signal $\\centernot\\implies$ Absolutely Integrable**.\n- **Conclusion:** Energy Signals and Absolutely Integrable Signals form **overlapping but distinct** sets!"
